{"id": "EUVD-2026-76663", "enisaUuid": "5dc0a2eb-7691-35a6-b457-5f8a2bee5024", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nx86/tdx: Fix off-by-one in port I/O handling\n\nhandle_in() and handle_out() in arch/x86/coco/tdx/tdx.c use:\n\n    u64 mask = GENMASK(BITS_PER_BYTE * size, 0);\n\nGENMASK(h, l) includes bit h. For size=1 (INB), this produces\nGENMASK(8, 0) = 0x1FF (9 bits) instead of GENMASK(7, 0) = 0xFF (8\nbits). The mask is one bit too wide for all I/O sizes.\n\nFix the mask calculation.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:52:05", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c6875423ad849ac234ab9812eb72f37ff8a490b4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/220011fe95fc78b2bc2d7d43893bc73957a5c811", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/222b7005e4519f633b4cd666226256abbab46a1a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c4a22154870813d10aa0b4c734a574c726f9d4b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb45f705c4440dd3c689328319b88dd28770bbb8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f63e656b1c679d32ac595de29d10c03efca6a25"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pv9x-wp8q-3x5j", "CVE-2026-89751"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c3cee06-c888-3869-81bb-d3c188ecacef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1160047d-fde2-3de8-9481-e594053deb3b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1e8cca9c-1549-3e0e-a5b0-5035e9c9889c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "03149948832a078f759022ed5b92e722d8d23c26 <c4a22154870813d10aa0b4c734a574c726f9d4b0"}, {"id": "48fe0261-9f02-3960-a183-a7a2b9fe9d96", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "03149948832a078f759022ed5b92e722d8d23c26 <222b7005e4519f633b4cd666226256abbab46a1a"}, {"id": "5d3e7513-8807-369f-8993-dbbb7e642ed3", "product": {"name": "Linux", 